Reason: when firstCollisionHit (patches 0056, 0067) finds the first instance self hits, the sorted walk starts at that
instance and ran all of the pair's tests on it again, nothing having run in between: for precise sprites that is a
second pixel scan of the same overlap, once per collision fired (in the mine chain ~66 a frame, 3.2 → 2.1 ms of pair
tests on the Wii). The walk now skips the tests for that one instance; every later instance is tested as before.
Upstream: Speed only, every platform. Retires this patch when merged.

